-- 0355 — the regional tier arrives: the subclass-tier rule, applied.
--
-- **The owner's direction, 2026-08-25: learn from the error, never patch the
-- instance.** Kunqu, Peking and Yue opera were missing while a corpus full of
-- their recordings refused every heading — and the cause was a rule, not
-- three rows: the recognised regional tier lives one subclass down. Peking
-- opera is `instance of: opera genre`, a subclass direct `P31` never reaches;
-- Italian cuisine had already taught the identical lesson to the cuisines
-- slice. So the genre slices now walk (`P31/P279*`) with the sitelink floor
-- as the depth guard, and the class the audit skipped — theatrical genre
-- (Q7777573) — becomes a slice of its own.
--
-- **The acceptance condition is that the trio arrives from the rule.** No
-- file names them: Peking opera, Kunqu, Yue opera — and Cantonese opera, Noh
-- and Kabuki beside them — all cleared the floor of a class-walk query. 540
-- concepts, 106 of them stage genres, twin-merged as ever, aliases with
-- locales (京剧, 崑曲, 越劇 are the whole point for this corpus).
--
-- **`medium:stage_genres` comes first** (0348's layer discipline), under
-- `hub:arts_live` beside — not inside — `medium:art_styles`: a stage genre
-- is a category of works, a movement is a style. New genre imports for the
-- walked slices land on their `medium:` layer nodes, because 0348 asserted
-- no genre hangs from a bare layered hub and a new import must not recreate
-- the state a migration asserted away.

